he dinar for years (removing 3 zeros), but it's been delayed due to: - Ongoing security/political instability - Wanting to time it with broader economic reforms - Central bank capacity issues - Fear of triggering inflation or panic if not executed smoothly **Bottom line:** It's not that it's impossible—it's that it's a costly, logistically complex undertaking that only makes sense when a country has enough economic and political stability to execute it well. Doing it just for convenience without fixing underlying issues would just delay the zeros coming back.
